From: Luca Bruni <lucbruni@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 18:22:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] clr: Enable OpenCL support for gfx8 (Polaris) GPUs

Two changes to allow gfx803 to work with the OpenCL runtime:

1. device.hpp: Remove the hardcoded check that blocked all GFX8 GPUs
   from the OpenCL (non-HIP) path in runtimeRocSupported(). The ISA
   table already marks gfx803 as runtimeRocSupported_=true; the extra
   versionMajor==8 gate was an unnecessary restriction.

2. rocdevice.cpp: Make HSA image extension queries (IMAGE_2D_MAX, etc.)
   non-fatal in populateOCLDeviceConstants(). On gfx803 these queries
   return errors from the HSA image extension, but that should not
   prevent the entire device from initializing. Image support is now
   gracefully disabled while all other compute capabilities remain.

Ref: https://github.com/ROCm/clr/issues/269
Made-with: Cursor
